Error [E0068]: this callable uses the retired result-arrow shape.
  --> tests/ui/E0927_retired_pure_callable.jet:1:21
    |
  1 | #Pure fn old_pure() => Int { return 2 }
    |                     ^^
 Why: a return type sits after the parameter list, and `->` introduces the body; an effect ceiling follows the return type
 Fix: write `fn name(...) Type -> body`, or `fn name(...) Type -[Effects]> { … }`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0068

Error [E0080]: A braced callable with a non-unit success result needs `->` before its body.
  --> tests/ui/E0927_retired_pure_callable.jet:1:28
    |
  1 | #Pure fn old_pure() => Int { return 2 }
    |                            ^
 Why: the body arrow marks a declared success value; unit and unit-fallible callables keep bare braces.
 Fix: write `fn name(...) Type -> { ... }`; keep `fn name(...) { ... }` and `fn name(...) Error! { ... }` bare.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0080

Error [E0927]: `#Pure` is retired
  --> tests/ui/E0927_retired_pure_callable.jet:1:1
    |
  1 | #Pure fn old_pure() => Int { return 2 }
    | ^^^^^
 Why: the applied-rule registry owns retired spellings and replacements
 Fix: write `=[]=>`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0927
